{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 29, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "## Lost (and Found) in Japan\n\nJapan. The word itself conjures images of ancient temples, bustling cities, and serene gardens. And let me tell you, the reality is even more captivating. I just returned from a whirlwind ten-day trip, and I’m already dreaming of going back.\n\nMy journey started in Tokyo, a sensory overload in the best way possible. Neon lights, incredible food stalls in Shibuya, and the peaceful Meiji Jingu Shrine – it's a city of contrasts. I spent hours wandering through the vibrant Harajuku district, marveling at the unique street style.\n\nFrom Tokyo, I took the Shinkansen (bullet train!) to Kyoto. The change of pace was instantly noticeable. Kyoto felt steeped in history, with its traditional wooden machiya houses and stunning temples like Kinkaku-ji (the Golden Pavilion). I even participated in a traditional tea ceremony, a truly calming experience.\n\nFood was, of course, a highlight. From delicate sushi and ramen to savory okonomiyaki, every meal was an adventure. I even braved trying fugu (pufferfish)!\n\nNavigating the train system was surprisingly easy, and the people were incredibly polite and helpful, even with my limited Japanese. \n\nJapan is a country that effortlessly blends tradition and modernity. It's a place where you can get delightfully lost in the moment, surrounded by beauty and kindness. Highly recommend adding it to your travel bucket list!\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.0011177966371178627}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -0.18502815067768097}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": "▁Found", "logprob": -0.0015026956098154187}, {"token": ")", "logprob": -0.1426810771226883}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁Japan", "logprob": -0.11408442258834839}, {"token": "\n\n", "logprob": -0.25964632630348206}, {"token"